</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F15.sf5" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2606.14416v1/res100c.png" id="A3.F15.sf5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/134;" width="215" height="134" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(e) </span>CIFAR-100, <math id="A3.F15.sf5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, local epochs = 5, ResNet-18</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A3.F15.sf6" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2606.14416v1/res100n.png" id="A3.F15.sf6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/134;" width="215" height="134" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(f) </span>CIFAR-100, <math id="A3.F15.sf6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, local epochs = 5, ResNet-18</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 15: </span>This figure displays the L2 norm of a client model and the cosine similarity between a client and the global model at each local epoch, for various algorithms implemented under cross-silo settings. The experiments were conducted with specific conditions (Dataset, Dirichlet alpha, local epoch, Model). The application of constraints consistently maintains the weight’s L2 norm throughout training. In the case of ResNet-18, which includes batch normalization layers, the weight norm is naturally consistent. Notably, a large change in cosine similarity during training with constraints suggests that local learning is dynamically evolving and not overly restricted.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
